WEBVTT


00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:05.530
This fabulous spiky
scarf is a Knit-1 design.

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:09.850
Impressive as it is, it
really isn't hard to knit.

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:16.990
The key is understanding that we're using
partial knitting or short rows to create

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:20.920
full pyramid shapes and
half pyramid shapes.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:23.400
Now don't be overwhelmed.

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:26.610
There are only two knitting sequences.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:33.330
The half pyramids allow us to alternate
the position of the full pyramids for the

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:34.050
design.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:36.240
Let's get started.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:42.300
We'll cast on 48 stitches with any
method and knit for a couple rows.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:46.470
The pattern tells us to start
with the carriage on the left.

00:00:48.365 --> 00:00:52.695
Now throughout the knitting, you'll
keep your carriage set to hold.

00:00:55.135 --> 00:01:01.655
We'll get started by knitting our first
pyramid over the left 24 needles, so we'll

00:01:01.655 --> 00:01:04.445
put the right 24 needles
into hold position.

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:15.660
Throughout this whole pattern, we'll
be placing needles in and out of hold

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:18.420
position - opposite the carriage

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:26.940
In order to keep the stitches from popping
off as you're knitting, the biggest

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:29.670
challenge is to keep
weight on the knitting.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:34.800
Either use weights, your fingers
or a combination of both.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:43.190
Start working the partial knitting by
pulling into hold the first needle that's

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:44.660
opposite the carriage.

00:01:50.289 --> 00:01:54.580
Keep putting one needle into hold
with every pass of the carriage.

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:09.419
You need to ensure on every row
that the stitches knit correctly.

00:02:15.325 --> 00:02:17.725
Now notice I'm not wrapping any needles.

00:02:18.415 --> 00:02:22.045
This creates the eyelets that
are a feature of this design.

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:02.940
Opposite the carriage keep putting needles
into hold until you have a single needle

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.049
in working position.

00:03:08.399 --> 00:03:15.390
And then begin returning needles back into
working position.Opposite the carriage

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:19.470
return one needle to work with
every pass of the carriage.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:39.620
Do this until all 24
needles are back in work.

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:50.200
Be sure to keep weight on those
stitches so they all knit correctly.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:52.060
They'll tend to pop up.

00:03:56.590 --> 00:04:02.350
Continue to put needles back into work,
one at a time, opposite the carriage until

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:05.470
all of those 24 needles are
back into working position.

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:21.930
Now notice on the last pass of the
carriage, I'm going to put two needles

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:23.400
back into working position.

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:24.990
It's just the way it works out.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:31.710
I've ended with my carriage on the
left and my first pyramid is complete.

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:36.120
I still have 24 needles in a
hold position on the right,

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:45.040
and I put some weight on
the stitches on the right.

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:47.650
It's time to start knitting.

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:48.910
The second pyramid.

00:04:51.375 --> 00:04:53.415
Now keeping that carriage set to hold.

00:04:53.715 --> 00:04:57.945
I'll put the needles in the right into
middle position, so they'll knit on the

00:04:57.945 --> 00:05:03.105
next pass of the carriage, but I'm going
to immediately start the partial knitting

00:05:03.255 --> 00:05:06.525
by keeping the first needle
in the right in hold.

00:05:07.885 --> 00:05:09.475
Knit across to the right.

00:05:10.465 --> 00:05:12.015
I didn't mean to complicate this.

00:05:12.495 --> 00:05:18.315
If you forgot to keep this one needle out
at this point, you can just un-knit it, or

00:05:18.315 --> 00:05:21.015
you could start your partial
knitting on the next row.

00:05:21.615 --> 00:05:22.965
Hang in there with me.

00:05:24.495 --> 00:05:31.155
We're going to be working on the right 24
needles, so I'm all done with the needles

00:05:31.155 --> 00:05:31.815
on the left.

00:05:31.845 --> 00:05:37.515
That first pyramid is finished, so we'll
put those needles into hold position.

00:05:37.725 --> 00:05:38.715
We're all done with them.

00:05:40.715 --> 00:05:46.175
Working over the right 24 needles, just
like before, opposite the carriage.

00:05:46.205 --> 00:05:47.855
I'll put one needle into hold.

00:05:48.815 --> 00:05:53.375
Paying attention to keep those stitches
knitting correctly, add weight, or use

00:05:53.375 --> 00:05:54.065
your fingers.

00:05:56.005 --> 00:05:57.505
Work your partial knitting.

00:05:57.775 --> 00:06:01.345
One needle to hold opposite
the carriage knit across.

00:06:01.525 --> 00:06:05.815
One needle to in hold opposite
the carriage knit across.

00:06:13.130 --> 00:06:16.580
Until there's only one needle
left in working position.

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:25.179
Then you'll begin to return needles into
work, one at a time opposite the carriage.

00:06:26.869 --> 00:06:27.830
Needle in work.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:28.849
Knit across.

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:31.340
Needle in work knitting across.

00:06:50.435 --> 00:06:55.445
You should have 24 needles in work,
and the second pyramid is complete.

00:07:00.265 --> 00:07:03.265
That's the first section of our repeats.

00:07:04.015 --> 00:07:11.185
For the next section, we're going to knit
a partial pyramid on each side with a full

00:07:11.185 --> 00:07:12.415
pyramid in the middle.

00:07:17.115 --> 00:07:20.625
We'll start by partial knitting
over 12 stitches this time.

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:24.540
The short rows are the same,
but we're only working.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:27.060
The increases in decreases on one side.

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:29.670
Carriage is on the right.

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:32.100
The carriage is still in hold.

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:38.450
Put all the needles into hold position
except the 12 needles right next to the

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:39.230
carriage.

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:46.690
As before, we'll put one needle opposite
the carriage into hold knit across, knit

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:50.090
back, put the next needle into hold.

00:07:50.415 --> 00:07:52.425
Knit across, knit back.

00:08:07.155 --> 00:08:10.575
Continue until there's only
one needle in working position.

00:08:11.775 --> 00:08:16.665
Then start the short row increases by
putting one needle back into work again.

00:08:17.969 --> 00:08:19.710
Always opposite the carriage.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:22.140
Knit across and back.

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:24.659
One needle into work.

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:26.580
Knit across and back.

00:08:39.710 --> 00:08:43.760
Repeat until all 12 needles
are back into working position.

00:08:45.555 --> 00:08:48.315
Can you see our first half pyramid?

00:08:49.005 --> 00:08:52.335
This is the start of the
second section of the scarf.

00:08:53.205 --> 00:08:57.585
Next is the center section,
and it will be a full pyramid.

00:08:58.605 --> 00:09:02.715
Now to keep things straight, I like
to use a pencil to mark my needle bed.

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:04.380
For this project.

00:09:04.469 --> 00:09:07.110
I'm going to mark the center 24 needles.

00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:09.120
To start the second pyramid,

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:13.290
put those center 24 needles into
middle positions, so they'll knit.

00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:16.920
Leave the left 12 needles in hold.

00:09:17.699 --> 00:09:19.260
We're going to do that next.

00:09:19.439 --> 00:09:24.250
Just leave those stitches in hold knit
across the needles and work, which is a

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:26.020
total of 36 needles.

00:09:28.209 --> 00:09:29.740
Now your carriage is on the left.

00:09:31.275 --> 00:09:35.325
We're done with those 12 half pyramid
needles that are on the right.

00:09:36.045 --> 00:09:37.695
We're all done with that little section.

00:09:37.695 --> 00:09:41.205
So put those 12 half pyramid
needles into hold position.

00:09:42.555 --> 00:09:45.495
Only the center 24 needles
are in working position.

00:09:46.065 --> 00:09:52.545
And we'll start the partial knitting and
creating a full pyramid . Opposite the

00:09:52.545 --> 00:09:53.025
carriage.

00:09:53.025 --> 00:09:54.695
Put one needle into a hold,

00:09:56.755 --> 00:09:57.685
knit across.

00:10:01.785 --> 00:10:02.865
Opposite the carriage.

00:10:02.865 --> 00:10:05.415
Put one needle into hold, knit across.

00:10:06.344 --> 00:10:07.334
Hang some weights.

00:10:09.425 --> 00:10:12.785
Can you see that this is the same
sequence that we started with?

00:10:12.905 --> 00:10:14.824
We're creating a full pyramid.

00:10:14.944 --> 00:10:19.115
There are 12 needles and hold on each side
of the work and we're just knitting in the

00:10:19.115 --> 00:10:19.625
center.

00:10:20.824 --> 00:10:25.865
Continue putting needles in hold on each
side until you've gotten all the way down

00:10:25.865 --> 00:10:27.665
to only one needle in work.

00:10:54.215 --> 00:10:59.055
Complete the pyramid by putting
needles back into work, one at a time.

00:11:00.435 --> 00:11:06.225
Opposite the carriage needle into work,
knit across .Needle under work, knit

00:11:06.225 --> 00:11:07.245
across needle.

00:11:07.245 --> 00:11:08.925
Needle into work knit across.

00:11:38.145 --> 00:11:41.105
Now this complete that
center full pyramid.

00:11:41.105 --> 00:11:43.665
End

00:11:49.605 --> 00:11:53.325
with the carriage and the
working yarn on the right.

00:11:57.265 --> 00:12:02.055
We'll now put the 12 needles in the
left into middle position so they knit.

00:12:02.455 --> 00:12:04.885
We'll pass the carriage
across to the left.

00:12:06.535 --> 00:12:07.945
We're on the home stretch.

00:12:15.470 --> 00:12:19.220
We're done with the center 24
needles and we'll put them in hold.

00:12:20.390 --> 00:12:24.050
The right 12 needles
are also still in hold.

00:12:25.070 --> 00:12:30.530
Now don't forget, the carriage remains
set to hold throughout this whole project.

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:33.530
Carriage is on the left.

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:38.250
Starting knitting a half pyramid
across the needles in work.

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:41.790
Opposite the carriage,
put a needle into hold.

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:43.740
Knit over and back.

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:45.780
Opposite the carriage,

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:47.160
put a needle into hold.

00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:48.930
Over and back.

00:12:49.770 --> 00:12:52.380
Repeat this until there's
one needle in work.

00:13:01.645 --> 00:13:07.495
Then return the needles back one at a
time, just like before, needle in work

00:13:08.245 --> 00:13:12.775
knit over, knit back, needle
in work knit over, knit back.

00:13:20.985 --> 00:13:23.395
You're going to end with
the carriage on the left.

00:13:25.775 --> 00:13:31.725
Put all the needles into middle position
or working position so that they all knit.

00:13:31.725 --> 00:13:37.545
We're going to knit one row all across all
of the needles and we will have completed

00:13:37.605 --> 00:13:39.705
one pattern repeat.

00:13:42.104 --> 00:13:46.305
We'll complete this sequence for
the desired length of the scarf.

00:13:47.444 --> 00:13:51.495
Section one has a full pyramid on the
left and a full pyramid on the right.

00:13:52.125 --> 00:13:56.775
Section two has a half pyramid on the
left and right, and a full pyramid in the

00:13:56.775 --> 00:13:57.314
center.

00:13:58.214 --> 00:14:01.245
You see how they're
alternating for the pattern?

00:14:01.694 --> 00:14:06.104
When your scarf is complete,
knit, a few rows bind off loosely.

00:14:06.510 --> 00:14:07.500
And you're all done.

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:12.120
Thanks to the folks at Knit-1 for
sharing this fun, fun pattern.

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:17.700
It's great practice for short row
shaping, and I'm sure you'll get lots of

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:18.960
compliments on your scarf.

00:14:19.770 --> 00:14:20.640
Happy knitting.